; THE HEADER-CANONICALIZATION WITNESS.
;
; GitHub sends `X-GitHub-Event: push`. An Oath handler asking for the header by
; the name GitHub documents gets NOTHING; asking for `X-Github-Event` gets the
; value. The Go backend's handler adapter puts requests through net/http, which
; canonicalizes header keys (each dash-separated token capitalized, the rest
; lowercased — so `GitHub` becomes `Github`), and that transformation is
; invisible in the Oath source, in the type, and in the guarantee.
;
; It fails SILENTLY and it fails OPEN in the shape that matters: a handler that
; branched on `(== (header-or hs "X-GitHub-Event" "-") "ping")` would be
; comparing against a header that never arrives, so the ping branch would be
; dead and every ping would take the other path. Nothing in the artifact's
; verdict would mention it.
;
; This exists so the fact is a RUNNABLE OBSERVATION rather than a comment:
;
;   oath put apps/github-webhook/hdr-probe.oath
;   oath build hdr-probe -o /tmp/hdr-probe && OATH_HTTP_ADDR=:8898 /tmp/hdr-probe &
;   curl -sS -X POST localhost:8898/ -H 'X-GitHub-Event: push' -d '{}'
;   MISS-as-documented|push|MISS-lowercase
;
; The middle field is the one that hits. If a future backend, or a change to the
; handler adapter, stops canonicalizing — or canonicalizes differently — this
; prints something else and apps/github-webhook/webhook.oath is wrong in a way
; no test of that file would catch.
;
; Recorded in docs/experiments/webhook-friction.md as the top-ranked TOOLING
; finding: the handler protocol has no header model, so an application has to
; encode one backend's normalization in its source.
(defn hdr-probe [] [(r Request)] Response
  (Resp 200 (Nil [(Pair Str Str)])
    (str-bytes (join-with "|"
      (Cons [Str] (header-or (req-headers r) "X-GitHub-Event" "MISS-as-documented")
        (Cons [Str] (header-or (req-headers r) "X-Github-Event" "MISS-go-canonical")
          (Cons [Str] (header-or (req-headers r) "x-github-event" "MISS-lowercase")
            (Nil [Str])))))))
  (prop always-200 [(r Request)] (== (match (hdr-probe r) ((Resp s h b) s)) 200)))
